Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and their possible usage  
• purchases.id : primary key that lets us identify each purchase batch  
• purchases.purchased : purchase date – drives the FIFO rule (earliest first)  
• inventory.purchase_id : links a stock row to the purchase batch it came from  
• inventory.product_id : the product in that location / batch  
• inventory.qty : quantity that was stored in that location / batch (supply side)  
• picking_line.order_id : tells which customer order a pick belongs to  
• picking_line.product_id : the product being picked  
• picking_line.qty : quantity that was actually picked from inventory  
• orderlines.order_id : quantity originally requested on the order line  
• orderlines.product_id : same product key – lets us compare ordered vs picked  
• orderlines.qty : quantity requested (demand side)  
• products.id : numeric product key  
• products.name : human readable product name (needed in result)  

Typical join / filter conditions we will need  
• picking_line.order_id  = orderlines.id  
• picking_line.product_id = orderlines.product_id  
• inventory.purchase_id   = purchases.id  
• inventory.product_id    = picking_line.product_id (and products.id)  
• Use MIN(purchases.purchased) to pick the FIFO lot first  
• Use the smaller of (orderlines.qty – qty already covered) and inventory.qty to decide overlap quantity  
• GROUP BY products.name to get one row per product  
• ORDER BY products.name  

Below are 10 exploratory queries (all limited to 20 rows) to understand the data before writing the final average‑pick‑percentage query.

```sql
--Description: 1. Distinct product ids that ever occurred in any picking line.
SELECT DISTINCT "product_id"
FROM "picking_line"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2. Map those product ids to their names.
SELECT DISTINCT p."id", p."name"
FROM "products" AS p
JOIN "picking_line" AS pl
  ON pl."product_id" = p."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3. Show ordered vs picked quantities for each order line (first 20 rows).
SELECT ol."order_id",
       ol."product_id",
       ol."qty"   AS "ordered_qty",
       pl."qty"   AS "picked_qty"
FROM   "orderlines"  AS ol
JOIN   "picking_line" AS pl
       ON pl."order_id"  = ol."order_id"
      AND pl."product_id" = ol."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4. List inventory rows with purchase date for the same products (first 20 rows).
SELECT inv."id"            AS "inv_row",
       inv."product_id",
       inv."qty"           AS "inv_qty",
       pur."purchased"     AS "purchase_date"
FROM   "inventory" AS inv
JOIN   "purchases" AS pur
       ON pur."id" = inv."purchase_id"
ORDER BY pur."purchased" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5. Earliest purchase date per product (helps to enforce FIFO).
SELECT inv."product_id",
       MIN(pur."purchased") AS "first_purchase_date"
FROM   "inventory" AS inv
JOIN   "purchases" AS pur
       ON pur."id" = inv."purchase_id"
GROUP BY inv."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6. Cumulative inventory (sum) per product to see total stock.
SELECT inv."product_id",
       SUM(inv."qty") AS "total_on_hand"
FROM   "inventory" AS inv
GROUP BY inv."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7. Cumulative picked quantity per product.
SELECT pl."product_id",
       SUM(pl."qty") AS "total_picked"
FROM   "picking_line" AS pl
GROUP BY pl."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8. Cumulative ordered quantity per product.
SELECT ol."product_id",
       SUM(ol."qty") AS "total_ordered"
FROM   "orderlines" AS ol
GROUP BY ol."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9. Join ordered and picked totals to compute a rough pick percentage.
SELECT prod."name",
       ord."total_ordered",
       pic."total_picked",
       ROUND(100.0 * pic."total_picked" / ord."total_ordered", 1) AS "pick_pct"
FROM  (
        SELECT "product_id", SUM("qty") AS "total_ordered"
        FROM   "orderlines"
        GROUP BY "product_id"
      )  AS ord
JOIN  (
        SELECT "product_id", SUM("qty") AS "total_picked"
        FROM   "picking_line"
        GROUP BY "product_id"
      )  AS pic
   ON pic."product_id" = ord."product_id"
JOIN "products" AS prod
   ON prod."id" = ord."product_id"
ORDER BY prod."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10. Show per‑order detailed FIFO overlaps: each pick row with the purchase date of the inventory it was taken from (helps verify FIFO logic).
SELECT pl."order_id",
       prod."name",
       pl."qty"                     AS "picked_qty",
       pur."purchased"              AS "inventory_purchase_date"
FROM   "picking_line" AS pl
JOIN   "inventory"    AS inv
         ON inv."location_id" = pl."location_id"
        AND inv."product_id"  = pl."product_id"
JOIN   "purchases"    AS pur
         ON pur."id" = inv."purchase_id"
JOIN   "products"     AS prod
         ON prod."id" = pl."product_id"
ORDER BY prod."name", pur."purchased", pl."order_id"
LIMIT 20;
```
